.TH COMMAND * 2014-04-08 "SequoiaDB" "Sequoiadb Method's Manual"
.ad l.ll 72.ce 1000
\fBdb.traceOn()\fR
.ce 0
.sp 2

.SH "NAME"

.sp 2
traceOn - Turn on the database engine program tracking.

.SH "SYNOPSIS"

traceOn(\fB<bufferSize>,[strComp],[strBreakPoint]\fR)

.SH "CATEGORY"

Sdb

.SH "DESCRIPTION"

.sp 2
Turn on the database engine program tracking.

.SH "PARAMETERS"

\fBbufferSize (int)\fR
.br
       The size of the tracked.
.sp 2
\fBstrComp (string)\fR
.br
       The module we specified.
.sp 2
\fBstrBreakPoint (String)\fR
.br
       Breake point.

.SH "RETURN VALUE"
.sp 2
On success, return void.
.sp 2
On error, exception will be thrown.
.sp 2
.SH "ERRORS"
.sp 2
when exception happen, use getLastError() to get the error code and use
getLastErrMsg() to get error message.
For more detial, please reference to Troubleshooting.

.SH "Examples"

.sp 2
Turn on the trace function of the database engine. Default is all
the modules. And track only the node that db connected.
.sp 2
>\ db.traceOn(\ 10000000\ );
.sp 2
Turn on the tracefunction of the database engine, and specify the
module's name to be traced and add a breakpoint to trace.
.sp 2
>\ db.traceOn(\ 10000000,\ "cls, dms, mth", "_dmsTempCB::init"\ ) ;
.sp 2
When the tracked module was blocked because of the breakpoint, you can use
traceResume() to wake up the module which was tracked and blocked.
.sp 2
>\ db.traceResume()
.sp 2
Using traceStatus() to view the tracking status of the current program.
.sp 2
>\ db.traceStatus()
.sp 2
Using traceOff() to turn off the database engine program tracking and export
tracking results to binary files.
.sp 2
>\ db.traceOff(\ "/opt/sequoiadb/trace.dump"\ )
.sp 2
Using traceFmt() to analysis the binary file.
.sp 2
>\ traceFmt(\ 0,\ "/opt/sequoiadb/trace.dump",\ "/opt/sequoiadb/trace_output"\ )
.sp 2